<title>HONG KONG: Magnum Int'l 1996 net loss HK$11.76 mln.</title>
<headline>Magnum Int'l 1996 net loss HK$11.76 mln.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended December 31</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   1.91 loss  vs  0.16 gain</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    nil	  vs  nil</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  5.34 gain  vs  13.71 gain</p>
<p>    Net			    11.76 loss vs  1.01 profit</p>
<p>    Turnover		     26.13	vs  51.69</p>
<p>    Company name		 Magnum International Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  June 18-26</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   N/A</p>
<p>NOTE - Magnum International is an electronics maker and stockbroker.</p>
<p>The company changed its financial year-end to December 31 from March 31. Comparative figures are for April 1 to December 31, 1995.</p>
<p>Net is after an exceptional gain on write-back of commissions payable and option fee income.</p>
<p>Total dividend for year is nil vs nil (nine months ended December 31, 1995).</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
